cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Bari"
    given-names: "Rchin"
title: "Riji: Desktop Colocalization and Live-Cell Image Analysis for Confocal Microscopy"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
url: "https://github.com/rcbweb/riji"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rcbweb/riji"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - "microscopy"
  - "colocalization"
  - "cellpose"
  - "live-cell analysis"
  - "cell viability"
  - "bioimage informatics"
  - "confocal"
  - "fluorescence quantification"
abstract: >-
  Riji is an open-source, reproducible desktop application and Python pipeline
  for multichannel confocal microscopy colocalization and live-cell image analysis.
  It integrates deep-learning cell segmentation (Cellpose), morphological viability scoring,
  human-in-the-loop validation, and automated publication-ready figure and statistical table generation.
